# tools/ales_reverse_witness.rish — reverse: turn the whole clip end for end, the plainest EXACT edit on the timeline (ALES104).
#
# Season: the Six-Season double-seat, Season C thread (Lotus · the creative suite) · waymark ALES · rung ALES104.
# Design read: active-designing/date/20260815/20260815-002711_fill-ales104-lotus-reverse.md
# Stands on: lotus/timeline.rye (ALES2 — the Clip and its buf/len/samples), lotus/meter.rye (ALES13 — the peak/RMS meter, used only to prove a permutation moves no
# loudness). Reverse is the "Reverse" menu item every editor and DAW ships, and it carries real creative charge: the reversed cymbal swell, the backwards reverb, the
# pre-echo lifted before a downbeat. Where ALES103's normalize changes every VALUE and no position, reverse changes every POSITION and no value — its exact mirror.
#
# lotus/reverse.rye walks the clip from both ends inward, swapping buf[i] with buf[len-1-i] until they meet — one in-place pass of len/2 swaps, no allocation. The crux is
# four laws. THE ORDER LAW: reverse lands a hand-reversed vector exactly, the first sample becoming the last. THE INVOLUTION LAW: reverse twice is the identity for any
# clip, so a mistaken reverse reverses back to the byte. THE PERMUTATION LAW: the length and the peak magnitude (re-measured through ALES13) are unchanged, since no
# value moves, only its seat. THE FIXPOINT LAW: an empty clip, a single-sample clip, and a palindrome are each their own reverse. The selftest proves all four.
#
# Run from the repository root:
#   rishi/bin/rishi run tools/ales_reverse_witness.rish

say "ales-reverse: Language EN — reverse is the Reverse menu item every editor and DAW ships: turn the whole clip end for end. It carries real creative charge — the reversed cymbal swell, the backwards reverb, the pre-echo lifted before a downbeat. Sample i and sample len-1-i trade seats, the first becoming the last, until the two ends meet in the middle."
say "ales-reverse: Style Radiant — the rule is stated positively: swap from both ends inward until they meet; the middle of an odd clip never moves; the length is untouched. Where ALES103's normalize changes every value and no position, reverse changes every position and no value — its exact mirror. The crux stands out as four laws: the order law (reverse lands the hand-reversed vector exactly), the involution law (reverse twice is the identity), the permutation law (length and peak unchanged), and the fixpoint law (empty, single, and palindrome each their own reverse)."
say "ales-reverse: Lens TAME — one mono clip of i16 PCM turned end for end in one in-place pass of len/2 swaps, no allocation and no second buffer; it rearranges existing samples and fabricates none, changes no length, and reads no byte past len; it names no span, so it forwards no EditError — total on any legal Clip; the permutation law is checked through ALES13's read-only meter (peak before equals peak after); siloed to lotus/, no real sample rate, no network, no keys, no funds, no device, no speaker."

let zig = "vendor/zig-toolchain/zig"
let bin = "lotus/bin/reverse"

let build = run ["sh" "-c" "mkdir -p lotus/bin && env RYE_ZIG=${zig} rye/bin/rye build lotus/reverse.rye -femit-bin=${bin}"]
assert build.ok else "ales-reverse: build failed — ${build.err}"

let outfile = "lotus/bin/reverse.out"
let selftest = run ["sh" "-c" "${bin} selftest > ${outfile} 2>&1"]
assert selftest.ok else "ales-reverse: selftest exited non-zero — see ${outfile}"

let shown = run ["sh" "-c" "cat ${outfile}"]
say "ales-reverse: ${shown.out}"

let green = run ["sh" "-c" "grep -q 'GREEN ales-reverse' ${outfile} && echo yes"]
assert (trim green.out) == "yes" else "ales-reverse: selftest did not print the GREEN ales-reverse line"
